- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests`

**How to implement.** The Mueller-matrix observation file, which the app writes and the `Mueller-matrix observations` profile reads (001 §K 'a Mueller-matrix observation profile (§Q, AT-2)'; 001 §Q AT-2 'written as kit data files … through the Mueller-matrix import profile, committed with the kit, and read back through the same profile; the test regenerates them from the seeds and requires the committed files byte-identical'; 'Data identity: the observations the study loads equal the harness's, exactly'; the S9.2 brief: normalized m00…m33 + absolute throughput + the configuration columns, in the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, and it also WRITES files). New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: `module LabFileImport` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `MuellerDataStore.fs`, one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` and no comment; its module doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `type KeyedObservation with static member observationFileText (observations : KeyedObservation list) : Result<KitFileText, ExperimentDataError>` writes the file: the header row `sample,cut,cut_tilt_rad,thickness_m,incidence_rad,azimuth_rad,observable,wavelength_nm,m00,m01,m02,m03,m10,m11,m12,m13,m20,m21,m22,m23,m30,m31,m32,m33,throughput` (the one place it is written), then one row per observation in order: the key's text; the cut's `value` and its `tilt` in radians (step 300); the thickness in metres; the incidence angle's and the azimuth's radians (`IncidenceAngle.value`, `SampleAzimuth.value`); the observable's `value`; the wavelength in nanometres, a `Nm` case's own number; the sixteen elements of `measured.normalized` (`MuellerInverse.fs:normalized`) in row order; and `measured.element 0 0`, the absolute throughput. Cells are joined by `,`, each row ends in `\n`, and no byte-order mark is written. Every number is `ToString("R", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`, the shortest text that reads back to the same double, so the same observations always write the same text. It answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the observation's 1-based position and key, and writes nothing, for a key that is empty or holds `,`, `"`, a carriage return or a line feed; an `Infinity` thickness; a `Mkm` wavelength, because the file records nanometres (`Fields.fs:WaveLength`); and a matrix whose `normalized` answers an `InversionError`. (2) `type KitFileText with member this.parseMuellerObservations : Result<KeyedObservation list, ExperimentDataError>` reads it: lines are split on `\n`, a trailing `\r` trimmed and blank lines skipped; a first line other than the header above is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming it; no row after it is `EmptyDataFileErr`; each row holds 25 cells, its numbers read by `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`, its cut through `SampleCut.tryOfWire` of the tag and the tilt, its observable through `Observable.tryOfWire` and its key as `DataRowKey` of the cell; the first row that fails is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming its line and cell. The configuration is `{ cut; thickness = Thickness (<metres> * 1.0<meter>); incidenceAngle = IncidenceAngle (Angle <radians>); azimuth = SampleAzimuth (Angle <radians>); observable; waveLength = WaveLength.nm (<nanometres> * 1.0<nm>) }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), the incidence built from its radians, not through `IncidenceAngle.create`, so the stored angle is kept bit for bit; `measured` is the matrix whose element (i, j) is `throughput * <the normalized element>`, its m₀₀ the throughput itself. That is the arithmetic `misreadAbsolute` builds an absolute matrix with (`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs:misreadAbsolute`), so such a matrix reads back element for element. No other member, option or format is added: the profile reads only this shape, and the app writes only through `observationFileText`. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs`, `module LabFileImportTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its two test-local observations are keyed `Z-cut` and `optic axis (A)`: a `ZCut` plate of `Thickness.mkm 100.0<mkm>` at `IncidenceAngle.create (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `SampleAzimuth.degree 22.5<deg>`, `ReflectedMueller`, `WaveLength.nm 632.8<nm>`; and a `TiltedCut (Angle 0.3141592653589793)` plate of the same thickness at `IncidenceAngle.normal`, `SampleAzimuth.degree 67.5<deg>`, `TransmittedMueller`, the same wavelength. Each matrix is built as `misreadAbsolute` builds one: a throughput t (0.8125, then 0.03) as m₀₀ and `t * nₖ` for the other elements, with nₖ = (−1)ᵏ (k + 1) / 17 at k = 4i + j. `the observation file writes each observation's configuration, normalized elements and throughput in one row`: the text has three lines, the first being the header, and the first row starts `Z-cut,1,0,`, has 25 cells, its ninth cell `1` (the normalized m₀₀) and its last `0.8125`. `an observation file reads back to the same observations, element for element, and writes back to the same text`: `parseMuellerObservations` of the text answers two keyed observations whose keys and configurations equal the written ones and each of whose sixteen `element i j` equals the written matrix's exactly, and `observationFileText` of them answers the same text. `an observation file of another shape, or one the profile cannot write, is refused`: a header without `m33` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the header; the header alone answers `EmptyDataFileErr`; a row of 24 cells and a row whose cut tag is `5` answer `MalformedDataFileErr` naming line 2; and writing an observation keyed `a,b`, one of `Thickness.Infinity`, one at `WaveLength.mkm 0.6328<mkm>` and one whose m₀₀ is 0 each answer `MalformedDataFileErr`. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.

**Acceptance.** After the observation file lands, `KeyedObservation.observationFileText` MUST write keyed observations as the header, the configuration, the normalized elements and the throughput in round-trip number text, refusing what it cannot write, and `KitFileText.parseMuellerObservations` MUST read such a file back to the same observations element for element; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the observation file writes each observation's configuration, normalized elements and throughput in one row`, `an observation file reads back to the same observations, element for element, and writes back to the same text` and `an observation file of another shape, or one the profile cannot write, is refused`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.
